<description>&lt;p&gt;Violence continues across South Sudan, with a grenade explosion killing four children and injuring two in Northern Bahr el Ghazal, and deadly clashes between Warrap and Lakes communities leaving 14 dead. The government is sending 25 young professionals to Brazil for specialized farming training and President Kiir traveled to Ethiopia, while Juba prepares to receive the Karuma hydropower plant by late 2026. UNHCR and South Sudan held talks to improve refugee support in Egypt, and the city council began road repairs and speed-bump installation within a week. Four individuals were sentenced to 14 years for a sexual assault case in Sherikat. Two battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihgFBVV95cUxNZ1BSWHJMaG1uRFFnYU5TUUIwMS14bzlFVkxuR21razB5d2Ytc3pkckhNWWNXQjI5OW15OTkwZnFVd0tULXdCS3RIVTNiX1doSTZTNVRTMWFwYkdNWHp2dXhURUFWTTJGNUNlR3NNb2hrUXE5b1puWjV6MnVQdnp0d2V3akhWdw?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Daily Monitor&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivwFBVV95cUxPMTVDcnRhUl9CT0FBMUdDU2xBM2drR1dZd3NlLWtUdEs1Y0pPbGx3alZKaDhSQ1p0cDlsOGNleUswWDdFa1hKeE12NGRyWWh2NmdCcXpmd1V0NTNMLXBkQm43TWNjNEllVU5lVUxZdzZZWUFmV1ZaUFczMzhSdzNLX09ia2x4cTFTUDB2SXAtc2RCSWRLczAzLVMybGhUQUdObTE1RlA4WS1aRzY2Q0dOZW85bmR6RzFhakZETEozbw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Daily Monitor&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxOY0U0WmNGM0FhU2Y0WUlGMkxlMkcwNkVYRzBkM2pkSy0wbHVDTXd0WE5OY3h0QjJPSjdIMlRTY3dlWjgtMGNXMFRJREVWd2laVHlNM2VmdlJheUNXOFJZMmVBRkE3aXp1ZUdycEVBang1ZzdndFdyYmI3SDBQWVlZTkNoaW9YRGNGcHFPZ0IwdzAyOEJramdCN0JsbHp1d1Q3eTFfNklna2VtNW_SAbABQVVfeXFMTWswVktIQ21tZjhyOVhHNHhUU09NRjdMYURTTmU